WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.824
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.924 --> 00:08.426
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.460 --> 00:11.996
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.030 --> 00:14.998
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.032 --> 00:18.500
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.535 --> 00:21.836
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.870 --> 00:23.403
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.438 --> 00:24.739
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.826 --> 00:27.378
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.380 --> 00:37.481
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Jeopardy Presents:</i>

00:37.515 --> 00:39.682
"The Best of Contestant Banter."

00:39.717 --> 00:42.585
So, Ben, it says here
you have a connection to milk.

00:42.619 --> 00:44.353
Yes, funny story.
I discovered recently

00:44.387 --> 00:46.088
that I have an allergy to milk.

00:46.122 --> 00:49.890
(chuckles) So I guess we won't
be eating any cheese around you.

00:49.925 --> 00:53.126
And Dennis, you once spent
a night in a tent?

00:53.160 --> 00:55.528
So, uh, what do you guys got
planned for the weekend?

00:55.563 --> 00:57.830
I don't know. I might sit
out in the front yard

00:57.864 --> 00:59.431
with a rake and
wave at cars.

00:59.466 --> 01:01.399
Yeah, and I found a hole
in my fence

01:01.433 --> 01:02.933
I was gonna maybe
stick stuff through.

01:02.967 --> 01:04.000
God, look at us.

01:04.035 --> 01:05.769
How'd we become so dull
and pathetic?

01:05.803 --> 01:06.769
You're right.

01:06.803 --> 01:08.270
I mean, we used
to have hobbies.

01:08.305 --> 01:09.804
Remember when I was
a horse whisperer?

01:09.839 --> 01:11.741
(whinnies)

01:13.509 --> 01:14.709
Shh, shh, shh.

01:14.744 --> 01:16.610
(whinnies, nickers)

01:18.012 --> 01:21.147
That's right.
I bet you're hungry.

01:21.181 --> 01:22.581
(softly):
It's okay.

01:24.450 --> 01:26.985
That calmed you down,
you (bleep) horse.

01:27.019 --> 01:28.519
Maybe it's time
the three of us

01:28.553 --> 01:29.987
do something exciting
to shake things up.

01:30.021 --> 01:31.588
Hey, now that's
a good idea, Joe!

01:31.622 --> 01:33.156
All right, okay,
I have two ideas.

01:33.190 --> 01:34.423
One that I think is awesome,

01:34.457 --> 01:35.824
and one that I think
is stupid.

01:35.859 --> 01:37.625
See if you can guess
which one is which.

01:37.659 --> 01:42.130
We could either
A) Rob a Mafia poker game,

01:42.164 --> 01:43.897
(flatly):
or B) Skydive.

01:43.931 --> 01:46.299
Skydiving, huh?
I'd be totally up for that!

01:46.334 --> 01:48.134
Yeah, I've always wanted
to try skydiving!

01:48.168 --> 01:50.735
Really? Eh, could be fun,
I guess.

01:50.770 --> 01:51.970
Besides, I haven't done
anything new

01:52.004 --> 01:53.971
since I learned
to use a palm frond.

01:54.005 --> 01:56.373
(whispers): So do I try
to match your speed?

01:56.408 --> 01:57.975
Yeah, just match my speed.

01:58.009 --> 01:59.642
And do we stagger
our waves

01:59.676 --> 02:01.177
or do 'em
at the same time?

02:01.211 --> 02:02.911
Um, they should've covered this
in orientation.

02:02.945 --> 02:05.379
Guards, have
the new guy executed!

02:05.414 --> 02:06.814
Am I the new guy?

02:10.284 --> 02:12.318
All right, we're almost at
our jumping altitude .

02:12.353 --> 02:13.753
Does anyone have
any questions?

02:13.788 --> 02:16.255
Yeah, I got one. Can I listen
to my iPod on the way down?

02:16.289 --> 02:17.756
Of course. Just as long

02:17.791 --> 02:19.657
as it's not
Tom Petty's "Free Fallin'".

02:19.691 --> 02:21.324
I'll just keep
it in my pocket.

02:21.359 --> 02:22.359
Any other questions?

02:22.393 --> 02:23.593
Let's do this!

02:23.628 --> 02:27.164
That wasn't a question.
Back of the line.

02:27.198 --> 02:28.664
Okay, let's do this!

02:28.698 --> 02:30.632
JOE:
Hey!

02:30.666 --> 02:32.066
Whoa, is that
Harrison Ford?

02:32.101 --> 02:33.567
Yeah. It said in
the brochure

02:33.601 --> 02:35.436
that he assists
with all the jumps.

02:35.470 --> 02:39.338
Get off my plane!
Get off my plane!

02:39.373 --> 02:41.473
Get off my plane!

02:41.507 --> 02:43.909
Oh, look, he even brought
Calista Flockhart with him.

02:43.943 --> 02:46.377
Uh, Peter, I think that's
just a piece of paper.

02:46.411 --> 02:47.978
Good, 'cause
she looked fat.

02:48.013 --> 02:50.146
HARRISON FORD:
Get off my plane!

02:50.181 --> 02:52.548
Get off my plane!
Get off my plane!

02:52.582 --> 02:54.183
All right!

02:54.217 --> 02:56.384
Yeah! This is amazing!

02:56.418 --> 02:57.853
I know,
it's unbelievable!

02:57.887 --> 03:00.154
Hey, guys, let's try
to re-create this feeling

03:00.189 --> 03:02.055
for the rest of our lives,
with drugs.

03:05.492 --> 03:07.059
Oh, it looks like
it's almost time

03:07.093 --> 03:09.093
for us to pull our cords.

03:09.128 --> 03:10.728
Wait, wait, guys.
How about this?

03:10.763 --> 03:13.097
Last one to open their chute
gets 20 bucks.

03:13.132 --> 03:14.832
Okay.
I'm in.

03:17.468 --> 03:19.001
Damn it!

03:20.870 --> 03:23.371
I'm dead already, Peter.

03:23.406 --> 03:25.039
You're looking
at a dead man.

03:25.073 --> 03:28.008
I might not even pull
the cord at all.

03:29.044 --> 03:31.010
(groans, whimpers)

03:32.947 --> 03:34.713
Holy crap, this is awesome!

03:34.747 --> 03:37.682
I haven't felt a rush like this
since I won that marathon!

03:39.317 --> 03:41.318
(runners screaming)

03:43.053 --> 03:44.354
I'm Bob Costas,

03:44.388 --> 03:45.788
here with Boston Marathon
winner Peter Griffin.

03:45.822 --> 03:47.122
Peter, how did you do it?

03:47.157 --> 03:48.324
I'll tell ya, Bob.

03:48.358 --> 03:50.225
I just got in my car
and drove it.

03:50.259 --> 03:52.759
And when there was a guy
in my way, I killed him.

03:56.129 --> 03:58.296
Kids, have you seen
your father?

03:58.331 --> 03:59.298
(phone rings)

03:59.333 --> 04:00.466
Hello?

04:00.501 --> 04:02.501
(air whooshing)
PETER: Is dinner almost ready?!

04:02.535 --> 04:03.902
Yes, Peter.
God, where are you?

04:03.936 --> 04:05.236
I can barely hear you.

04:05.270 --> 04:07.404
Pull back my chair
ever so slightly.

04:09.874 --> 04:11.940
(sighs)
Daddy's home.

04:14.143 --> 04:17.845
All right, it's 4:59.
In just a few seconds,

04:17.880 --> 04:21.014
all the unreturned library books
will be officially late.

04:22.450 --> 04:25.851
The wieners was already drawed
in the books when I got 'em.

04:28.053 --> 04:32.390
"Libra: A strange man will
drop into your life." Hmm.

04:35.326 --> 04:39.227
"Pisces: Be careful
at work today."

04:40.796 --> 04:42.830
♪

04:47.502 --> 04:50.003
Go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go...

04:50.037 --> 04:52.671
<i>Aw! He so shoulda died!
This is bullcrap!</i>

04:52.705 --> 04:54.172
Stop smiling.

04:54.207 --> 04:56.641
90% of the people
playing this are pooping.

04:59.978 --> 05:02.078
Hey, Lois, when are you
gonna do the laundry?

05:02.113 --> 05:03.680
I got, like, six
parachutes in there.

05:03.714 --> 05:05.874
Peter, those things are choking
up the washing machine.

05:05.882 --> 05:07.382
Oh, so now I got you
a bad washing machine

05:07.416 --> 05:08.850
for Christmas.

05:08.884 --> 05:09.918
Little tip, Stewie:

05:09.952 --> 05:11.885
Love dies, and
that's okay.

05:11.920 --> 05:14.620
I write down all his advice
in a little notebook.

05:14.655 --> 05:16.822
Yesterday's was, "I've
never seen a pigeon die

05:16.857 --> 05:18.057
"from eating food
on the ground,

05:18.091 --> 05:19.891
so what's the big whoop?"

05:19.926 --> 05:22.060
Peter, this skydiving thing
has gotta stop.

05:22.094 --> 05:23.561
You've destroyed half
the neighborhood.

05:23.595 --> 05:25.929
And I'm afraid you're
gonna really hurt yourself.

05:25.963 --> 05:26.963
I'm sorry, Lois.

05:26.997 --> 05:28.665
But skydiving is
who I am now.

05:28.699 --> 05:30.533
It's like they say,
fish gotta swim,

05:30.568 --> 05:33.302
birds gotta fly,
and gay guys gotta criticize

05:33.336 --> 05:35.103
the host of the party
behind his back.

05:35.138 --> 05:37.038
Oh, my God, look,
a bowl of M&M's.

05:37.072 --> 05:38.605
What are we, six?

05:38.639 --> 05:40.674
I know. And remind me
to get the recipe

05:40.708 --> 05:42.207
for those chopped-up
hot dogs.

05:42.242 --> 05:43.542
(both laugh)

05:43.577 --> 05:46.145
Oh, my God, Josh,
this party is so amazing!

05:46.179 --> 05:49.213
Everything is perfect!
We're having so much fun!

05:49.248 --> 05:52.182
Oh, thanks! I'm so glad
you guys could make it!

05:52.216 --> 05:53.917
Come on. He saw us.
Let's go.

05:56.954 --> 05:58.787
First time?

05:58.821 --> 06:00.088
(nervously):
Yeah. You?

06:00.122 --> 06:02.791
(laughs) No.
No, not my first time.

06:03.792 --> 06:05.726
Thanks for the lift, Gil.

06:05.760 --> 06:07.460
I think I'll take
the express down.

06:10.196 --> 06:12.531
♪

06:22.039 --> 06:24.974
(inhales deeply, sighs)

06:25.008 --> 06:27.141
Ah, just as gorgeous as ever.

06:27.176 --> 06:30.477
Actually puts me in the mind
to write a spoken word poem.

06:30.511 --> 06:32.779
Am I falling or am I flying?

06:32.814 --> 06:35.615
Am I living or am I dying?

06:35.649 --> 06:37.983
O, Great Spirit, free me

06:38.017 --> 06:40.785
from the bonds of gravity
and criticism.

06:40.820 --> 06:42.886
Deliver me
from my greatest enemy.

06:42.921 --> 06:44.621
His name is Peter.

06:44.655 --> 06:48.157
More specifically,
Peter's Shyness In Public.

06:48.192 --> 06:49.759
O, Great Spirit,

06:49.793 --> 06:52.361
why do I hold myself back
in such situa...?

06:52.395 --> 06:54.528
Oh, (bleep) (bleep)
the ground!

06:54.563 --> 06:57.697
(gasps) Damn it!

06:57.732 --> 06:58.999
The Eiffel Tower?

06:59.033 --> 07:00.766
Oh, cool, I'm in Paris!

07:00.800 --> 07:03.702
MAN: Hey, look at that douchebag
who got stabbed in the butt!

07:03.737 --> 07:06.537
Aw, crap, I'm in Vegas.

07:12.770 --> 07:14.671
Well, Peter, I'm glad
you're all right,

07:14.673 --> 07:17.274
but I hope this is the end
of your skydiving career.

07:17.308 --> 07:18.409
Yeah, I'm sorry, Lois.

07:18.443 --> 07:20.309
You know, when I thought
I was gonna die,

07:20.344 --> 07:22.678
I saw my whole life flash
before my eyes,

07:22.712 --> 07:25.413
<i>and we did way too much
Star Wars crap.</i>

07:25.447 --> 07:28.181
I should get the kids home.
It's way past dinner.

07:28.215 --> 07:30.016
What she really means is

07:30.051 --> 07:31.850
that it's shaky Mommy's
white wine time.

07:31.885 --> 07:34.054
Let's go, kids! Come on!
We really gotta go, kids.

07:34.088 --> 07:35.220
Let's go! Come on!

07:35.255 --> 07:38.022
Excuse me. Now that
your family is gone,

07:38.057 --> 07:40.358
would you mind if
we turn on the TV?

07:40.392 --> 07:42.526
Oh, hey. I didn't know
anyone was here.

07:42.560 --> 07:43.959
I, uh, I was just kidding

07:43.994 --> 07:45.861
when I told my family
I loved 'em.

07:45.896 --> 07:47.028
I am Mahmoud.

07:47.063 --> 07:49.998
I'm Peter. You know,
I never seen a hat

07:50.032 --> 07:52.033
like that before,
so I'm very scared of it.

07:52.068 --> 07:53.567
No, this is just
a taqiyah.

07:53.601 --> 07:55.302
It's a traditional
Muslim prayer cap.

07:55.336 --> 07:57.937
Oh. Hey, you know who'd look
funny wearing one of those?

07:57.971 --> 07:59.305
The Monopoly guy.

07:59.338 --> 08:01.740
(laughs) Correct!

08:01.774 --> 08:04.042
Go directly to jail
and convert to Islam!

08:04.077 --> 08:06.143
(laughs)
'Cause they do that!

08:06.178 --> 08:08.778
(chuckles weakly)
Yes, that is what I intended.

08:08.813 --> 08:10.346
Hey, you're all right,
Mahmoud.

08:10.381 --> 08:11.648
You, too, Peter.

08:11.682 --> 08:13.348
So, what do you
wanna watch?

08:13.383 --> 08:15.650
Well, if you turn on
Channel 14,

08:15.684 --> 08:18.019
<i>we can probably catch the end
of Muslim Looney Tunes.</i>

08:18.053 --> 08:20.188
(upbeat Middle Eastern
music plays)

08:20.222 --> 08:21.588
(stuttering)

08:21.622 --> 08:23.323
As a pig, I am very dirty

08:23.357 --> 08:25.791
and should not be touched
by humans.

08:28.994 --> 08:31.028
So, how was
the hospital, Peter?

08:31.062 --> 08:32.663
Oh, my God,
that place was incredible.

08:32.697 --> 08:35.799
They have this one jar, whole
thing was full of cotton balls.

08:35.834 --> 08:38.701
It's amazing how far
medical technology has come.

08:38.736 --> 08:40.902
Well, sure is good
to have you back.

08:40.937 --> 08:42.571
Joe is, uh...
(clears throat)

08:42.605 --> 08:45.506
chattier than you'd think
he'd be when you're not here.

08:45.540 --> 08:46.606
Look, I'm just saying

08:46.640 --> 08:48.608
if "pro" is the opposite
of "con",

08:48.642 --> 08:50.310
what is the opposite
of "progress"?

08:50.344 --> 08:51.377
Think about it.

08:51.412 --> 08:52.678
You know, I actually had

08:52.712 --> 08:54.179
a pretty good time in
the hospital.

08:54.214 --> 08:55.880
I even made a new friend.
You did?

08:55.914 --> 08:57.014
Yeah, his name's Mahmoud.

08:57.049 --> 08:59.683
In fact, I told him to swing by
if he had time.

08:59.717 --> 09:00.717
It's "congress."

09:00.752 --> 09:02.017
Hello, Peter!

09:02.052 --> 09:04.321
Oh, hey! You made it!
Hey, guys, this is Mahmoud.

09:04.355 --> 09:06.088
Mahmoud, this is Brian,
Quagmire and Joe.

09:06.123 --> 09:07.123
Hello.
Hi, there.

09:07.157 --> 09:08.456
Hey, there.
Hello. How are you?

09:08.491 --> 09:09.691
Have a seat.

09:09.725 --> 09:11.725
Any friend of Peter's is
a friend of ours.

09:11.760 --> 09:13.994
Hey, Mahmoud, you know,
I'm actually glad you're here.

09:14.028 --> 09:15.528
Settle an argument
we were having earlier.

09:15.562 --> 09:16.896
Which Spanish chick has
better jugs:

09:16.930 --> 09:18.797
Salma Hayek
or the other one?

09:18.831 --> 09:21.299
Oh, but I do not pay
attention to such things.

09:21.334 --> 09:22.768
I am married.
What?

09:22.802 --> 09:24.235
Okay, well,
how about this, Mahmoud?

09:24.269 --> 09:26.103
You know "progress" has
the word "pro" in it, right?

09:26.138 --> 09:27.337
Shut up, Joe!

09:27.371 --> 09:29.639
Hey, you guys, come on.
Let's get the man a drink.

09:29.673 --> 09:30.739
What are you having?

09:30.774 --> 09:32.307
How about a ginger ale?

09:32.342 --> 09:35.177
But if you'll excuse me,
right now I have to go

09:35.211 --> 09:37.879
bring great shame to myself
by using the restroom.

09:37.913 --> 09:39.380
Isn't he great?

09:39.414 --> 09:40.380
No, he's weird.

09:40.414 --> 09:41.782
Why'd he order
a ginger ale?

09:41.816 --> 09:43.682
And who the hell doesn't
look at jugs?

09:43.717 --> 09:45.384
Yeah, and he's got
his cell phone clipped

09:45.418 --> 09:48.186
to his belt like he's some
kind of big shot on vacation.

09:48.220 --> 09:50.321
Oh, I see what's going on.

09:50.356 --> 09:52.456
You guys are uncomfortable with
Mahmoud because he's Muslim.

09:52.490 --> 09:54.291
What? What are you
talking about?

09:54.325 --> 09:56.259
This is your post-9/11 racism
talking.

09:56.293 --> 09:58.760
I, for one, think it's great
that Peter has enough

09:58.795 --> 10:00.896
of an open mind
to have a Muslim friend.

10:00.930 --> 10:03.964
You know, a lot of dogs
just sit outside, tied to poles.

10:03.999 --> 10:05.466
Look, Mahmoud's my friend, okay?

10:05.500 --> 10:08.334
So he's Muslim.
Every culture has its quirks.

10:08.369 --> 10:10.303
Italian guys talk
with their hands a lot,

10:10.337 --> 10:11.804
Irish guys drink a lot,

10:11.838 --> 10:14.505
black guys change their shirts
while they tell you a story.

10:14.540 --> 10:16.741
So, how's Bernadette?
She's all right.

10:16.775 --> 10:18.375
She's taking interior
design classes

10:18.409 --> 10:19.976
down at the
community college.

10:20.011 --> 10:21.845
I mean, she's good at
haircutting and everything.

10:21.879 --> 10:24.079
They gave her the chair
right by the door.

10:24.114 --> 10:25.614
But I guess now
she wants

10:25.649 --> 10:27.515
to hang plates on the
wall or whatever.

10:27.550 --> 10:29.250
And you know she gained
the weight back

10:29.285 --> 10:30.250
from the Lap-Band,
right?

10:30.285 --> 10:31.919
That Bernadette
and her pie.

10:31.953 --> 10:33.386
You know it, brother.

10:33.420 --> 10:35.889
Okay, I'm gonna go eat this steak
in the bathroom.

10:35.924 --> 10:38.024
Thanks for getting
dinner, man.

10:41.060 --> 10:44.028
(house music thumping, blaring)

10:44.062 --> 10:46.830
Wow, this place is
really cool, Mahmoud.

10:46.864 --> 10:49.198
It's like ear-bloodening
sounds had sex

10:49.232 --> 10:51.934
with nose-bloodening smells
and this is their baby.

10:51.968 --> 10:53.735
I am glad
you are enjoying yourself.

10:53.770 --> 10:56.070
Would you like some
of my meat fooshnoosh?

10:56.104 --> 10:58.505
It's a chicken that has
been yelled at for two hours

10:58.539 --> 11:00.340
and then run over
by a Mercedes.

11:00.374 --> 11:02.107
Mmm! Mmm! Oh!

11:02.142 --> 11:04.175
You can really taste
the fear in the chicken.

11:04.210 --> 11:05.276
You know, Peter,

11:05.311 --> 11:06.979
a lot of people are
not as accepting

11:07.013 --> 11:08.580
of Muslim culture
as you are.

11:08.614 --> 11:10.547
Well, I think everything
about it is the best.

11:10.582 --> 11:11.782
Like this hookah.

11:11.816 --> 11:13.350
I mean, who doesn't want
to sit around a table

11:13.384 --> 11:15.384
with a bunch of guys and
suck on the same thing?

11:19.155 --> 11:22.290
Mmm, it's like smoking
my grandfather's jacket.

11:22.325 --> 11:24.358
Man, I wish I could stay
here all night, Mahmoud.

11:24.392 --> 11:25.693
But I'm supposed
to pick up

11:25.727 --> 11:27.047
the dry cleaning
before it closes.

11:27.061 --> 11:28.661
I killed a mouse
with my tie.

11:28.696 --> 11:29.695
Nonsense.

11:29.729 --> 11:31.196
I'll have my wife
pick it up for you.

11:31.231 --> 11:32.496
What?
She'd do that?

11:32.531 --> 11:34.632
Oh, absolutely.

11:34.666 --> 11:37.001
I need you to run an errand
for my friend Peter.

11:37.035 --> 11:38.035
Of course.

11:38.070 --> 11:39.736
Anything for you,
husband.

11:40.872 --> 11:42.037
That was amazing.

11:42.072 --> 11:43.772
She just listened
to everything you said.

11:43.807 --> 11:45.006
Of course she listened.

11:45.040 --> 11:46.074
In Muslim culture,

11:46.108 --> 11:47.876
wives are much more obedient.

11:47.910 --> 11:49.409
No way!
That's awesome!

11:49.444 --> 11:50.844
So wait, let me
get this straight:

11:50.879 --> 11:52.512
Sweet hat, obedient wife,

11:52.547 --> 11:54.847
and I get to shout
"Admiral Akbar"

11:54.882 --> 11:55.915
when I do stuff?

11:55.949 --> 11:58.783
You, sir, have got
yourself a Muslim.

12:04.388 --> 12:05.555
Peter, where
are you going?

12:05.589 --> 12:07.089
And why are you
dressed like that?

12:07.123 --> 12:08.958
Well, Lois, I happen
to be a Muslim now,

12:08.993 --> 12:10.692
which means I'll be
spending a lot of my time

12:10.727 --> 12:12.895
in mostly-empty cafes,
watching soccer

12:12.929 --> 12:14.729
on an eight-inch
black-and-white TV.

12:14.763 --> 12:16.563
Yes! The team I like
is kicking it!

12:16.597 --> 12:18.465
Oh no! The team I don't like
is kicking it!

12:18.499 --> 12:20.499
Yes! The team I like
is kicking it again!

12:20.533 --> 12:22.401
I will celebrate
with finger cymbals.

12:22.435 --> 12:24.603
(chiming)

12:24.638 --> 12:25.870
Hey, is that for real,

12:25.905 --> 12:28.939
that-that "Diarrhea Only" sign
on your bathroom?

12:31.975 --> 12:33.676
Peter, this is my friend Omar.

12:33.710 --> 12:35.543
He can teach you many things
about our faith,

12:35.578 --> 12:36.978
including how to ululate.

12:37.013 --> 12:38.680
What's that?
It's this:

12:38.714 --> 12:39.915
(rapidly trilling
vocalization)

12:39.949 --> 12:41.882
Oh, my God!
That's terrifying.

12:41.917 --> 12:43.117
I don't know if
I'm ready for that.

12:43.151 --> 12:44.450
No, Peter, it's okay.

12:44.485 --> 12:46.419
Just sing the
beginning of "La Bamba,"

12:46.453 --> 12:47.984
but don't say the
"La Bamba" part.

12:48.009 --> 12:48.987
Oh, okay.

12:48.988 --> 12:50.255
(rapidly trilling vocalization)
Yes, good job!

12:50.290 --> 12:51.455
You're doing it!
♪ Bamba.

12:51.490 --> 12:52.924
Ooh, so close.

12:54.893 --> 12:57.594
All right, Lois,
I'm off to the bazaar.

12:57.628 --> 12:58.595
What do you mean?

12:58.629 --> 12:59.596
You mean the market?

12:59.630 --> 13:00.663
Yeah, the bazaar.

13:00.697 --> 13:01.864
Well, if you're
going to the market,

13:01.898 --> 13:03.098
can you pick
up some cereal,

13:03.133 --> 13:04.412
some butter, and
a loaf of bread?

13:04.433 --> 13:05.767
I'll see what
they have.

13:05.801 --> 13:07.567
All right, Lois.

13:07.602 --> 13:09.203
Here's six cobras,
a bolt of silk,

13:09.238 --> 13:10.304
and a ram's horn.

13:10.338 --> 13:11.405
Peter, what the hell?

13:11.439 --> 13:13.472
Hey, can you help me
with the 20 paper bags

13:13.507 --> 13:14.907
of dates I got in the car?

13:14.942 --> 13:17.275
Why the hell would you
get 20 bags of dates?

13:17.310 --> 13:19.410
The monkey in the little
vest who was selling them

13:19.444 --> 13:20.678
happened to be
very persuasive.

13:20.712 --> 13:21.779
(sighs)
You know what?

13:21.813 --> 13:22.779
Fine.

13:22.813 --> 13:24.381
I'm just gonna
assume this will pass,

13:24.416 --> 13:27.450
like your "everywhere is a
racquetball court" phase.

13:37.491 --> 13:38.857
(Peter gasping)

13:38.892 --> 13:40.793
So, Mike, now that you've
thoroughly kicked my butt

13:40.827 --> 13:42.628
all over the court,
what do you say we take

13:42.662 --> 13:44.729
one quick second to talk
about the Wichita account?

13:44.763 --> 13:46.965
And let me assure you,
my racquetball game

13:46.999 --> 13:49.633
is no indication of how we do
business here at J.T. Stern.

13:49.667 --> 13:50.633
(chuckles)

13:50.667 --> 13:52.368
Okay, zero serving zero.

13:54.738 --> 13:56.172
I have to say, Peter,

13:56.206 --> 13:57.605
I am impressed by how much

13:57.640 --> 13:59.140
you have committed
yourself to Islam.

13:59.175 --> 14:00.407
Are you kidding?
It's awesome.

14:00.442 --> 14:02.109
I even started wearing
leather sandals

14:02.143 --> 14:03.576
with way-too-long
toenails.

14:03.610 --> 14:05.211
See how the big ones
are getting yellow?

14:05.245 --> 14:07.145
Ah, yes, very Muslim.

14:07.180 --> 14:09.547
Listen, Peter, some
friends of mine and I

14:09.581 --> 14:10.849
are getting
together tonight

14:10.883 --> 14:12.717
and we wanted to invite
you to join us.

14:12.751 --> 14:14.685
O.M.A.

14:14.720 --> 14:15.986
I am so there!

14:16.020 --> 14:17.554
Whose crappy van
should we take?

14:17.588 --> 14:18.988
Actually, we are
meeting here.

14:19.022 --> 14:20.923
Follow me.

14:22.658 --> 14:23.624
Oh, hey, you guys.

14:23.659 --> 14:24.993
Hey, is anyone
gonna object

14:25.027 --> 14:26.828
if I pick my nose
with a dagger?

14:26.862 --> 14:28.295
Mahmoud,
who is this man?

14:28.329 --> 14:29.596
Why would you
bring him here?

14:29.630 --> 14:31.263
Do not worry.
This is Peter.

14:31.298 --> 14:32.598
He believes
in our cause.

14:32.632 --> 14:34.032
How can
you be sure?

14:34.066 --> 14:35.066
Give him the test.

14:37.335 --> 14:38.435
Who is better?

14:38.470 --> 14:40.704
Hulk Hogan or the Iron Sheik?

14:40.739 --> 14:43.040
Um, the Iron Sheik?

14:43.074 --> 14:44.874
Okay. He is one of us.

14:44.908 --> 14:46.009
I told you.

14:46.043 --> 14:47.809
Look at him,
he is the perfect man

14:47.844 --> 14:49.910
to help us blow up
the Quahog Bridge.

14:49.945 --> 14:50.911
(makes car noises)

14:50.946 --> 14:52.580
(imitates explosion)

14:52.614 --> 14:53.913
Ah! Oh my God!

14:53.948 --> 14:54.914
Everybody down!

14:54.949 --> 14:56.149
(imitates gunfire)

14:56.183 --> 14:58.418
So are these toys just, like,
to take?

15:04.840 --> 15:06.940
Hey, guys, what football
team should I like?

15:06.974 --> 15:08.308
Mahmoud says
we all need

15:08.342 --> 15:09.975
to act like we're fans
of American football

15:10.009 --> 15:13.579
so we seem less...
b-buh... buhspicious.

15:13.613 --> 15:15.012
What?
What are you talking about?

15:15.047 --> 15:16.414
I'm talking about Mahmoud.

15:16.448 --> 15:18.315
You know, I actually feel
really bad for him.

15:18.349 --> 15:21.350
Did you know he knew 19 guys
who died on 9/11?

15:21.385 --> 15:22.685
I mean, what are the odds?

15:22.719 --> 15:23.986
Peter, I think
you joined

15:24.020 --> 15:25.420
a terrorist
sleeper cell.

15:25.454 --> 15:26.889
What?! That's crazy.

15:26.923 --> 15:28.690
Look, I'm gonna
call Mahmoud right now

15:28.724 --> 15:30.158
on this cell
phone he gave me.

15:30.192 --> 15:30.958
He'll tell you.

15:30.992 --> 15:32.626
(keypad beeping)

15:32.660 --> 15:33.760
(explosion, glass shattering)

15:33.794 --> 15:34.827
Damn phone's busted.

15:34.862 --> 15:35.895
Maybe I dialed wrong.

15:35.929 --> 15:37.729
(keypad beeping)

15:37.764 --> 15:39.297
(explosion, people screaming)

15:39.332 --> 15:41.165
Peter, please stop trying
to call Mahmoud.

15:41.199 --> 15:42.334
This is very
serious.

15:42.368 --> 15:43.801
Your friends
are terrorists.

15:43.835 --> 15:45.035
Think about it.

15:45.070 --> 15:46.469
They're... they're
meeting in secret,

15:46.504 --> 15:48.304
they're creating
cover stories...

15:48.339 --> 15:49.872
Oh, my God, you're right!

15:49.906 --> 15:51.807
See, I told you
Mahmoud was bad news!

15:51.841 --> 15:53.341
Those guys are
all bad news.

15:53.375 --> 15:54.776
Hang on there,
Quagmire.

15:54.810 --> 15:56.844
Just because these few
guys are terrorists

15:56.879 --> 15:58.379
doesn't mean
all Muslims are.

15:58.414 --> 16:00.781
Every ethnic group
has their nut-jobs.

16:00.815 --> 16:02.948
We have the Unabomber,
Timothy McVeigh,

16:02.983 --> 16:05.016
and even that fat guy
at the Atlanta Olympics

16:05.050 --> 16:06.718
who didn't do it,
but he looked mean,

16:06.752 --> 16:08.085
so we said he did.

16:08.119 --> 16:10.239
Joe, you don't get to talk
about the regular Olympics.

16:10.255 --> 16:11.854
Well, I gotta go
down there right now

16:11.889 --> 16:13.524
and tell Mahmoud we can't
be friends anymore.

16:13.558 --> 16:14.657
Wait a minute, Peter.

16:14.691 --> 16:16.759
This could actually
be an opportunity.

16:16.794 --> 16:18.627
You're already
in their group.

16:18.661 --> 16:19.961
They trust you.

16:19.996 --> 16:22.329
If you can find out what
they're planning next,

16:22.364 --> 16:25.031
we might actually be able
to stop an act of terror.

16:25.065 --> 16:26.433
You'd be a hero.

16:26.467 --> 16:29.068
Well, I...
I could try.

16:29.103 --> 16:30.702
I mean, I am a
pretty good actor.

16:30.737 --> 16:32.271
Remember how upset
I seemed to get

16:32.305 --> 16:33.738
when Lois said she
was leaving town

16:33.772 --> 16:35.273
with the kids
for a few days?

16:35.307 --> 16:37.641
Oh, my God, I'm gonna
miss you guys so much.

16:37.675 --> 16:39.276
Don't forget to call
and let me know

16:39.309 --> 16:41.310
exactly when
you'll be back.

16:41.344 --> 16:42.344
Get out.

16:46.649 --> 16:48.216
Okay, you're all set.

16:48.250 --> 16:51.118
Remember, we'll be in the van
listening to everything,

16:51.152 --> 16:52.385
so if anything goes wrong,

16:52.419 --> 16:53.886
we'll pull you right
out of there.

16:53.921 --> 16:55.020
Don't you worry, Joe.

16:55.054 --> 16:56.721
I'll blend in
like a chameleon

16:56.756 --> 16:58.557
in Courtney
Love's crotch.

16:58.591 --> 17:00.158
Oh my God!

17:00.193 --> 17:01.425
Where did you
just come from?

17:01.460 --> 17:04.561
A very, very
bad hiding place.

17:07.997 --> 17:09.998
Okay, before we get started,

17:10.033 --> 17:11.899
I have an announcement
from headquarters.

17:11.934 --> 17:13.535
"No more shorts."

17:13.570 --> 17:16.037
And this isn't coming from me,
this is management.

17:16.071 --> 17:17.537
This is about me, isn't it?

17:17.572 --> 17:18.905
They don't name names.

17:18.940 --> 17:22.408
They just say,
"No more shorts," okay?

17:22.442 --> 17:24.175
All right, this is our target.

17:24.210 --> 17:25.276
The Quahog Bridge.

17:25.311 --> 17:26.944
We loaded a van
with explosives,

17:26.978 --> 17:28.580
which we will drive
to the bridge and...

17:28.614 --> 17:30.214
Wait a minute-- explosives?

17:30.248 --> 17:32.249
Is this not improv class?

17:32.283 --> 17:32.915
No.

17:32.950 --> 17:33.916
Is...

17:33.951 --> 17:35.017
is this improv?

17:35.052 --> 17:36.418
Are you doing improv?

17:36.452 --> 17:38.253
No. Now get out that door!

17:41.523 --> 17:42.889
The real door!

17:44.459 --> 17:45.859
Yes, I have a question:

17:45.893 --> 17:47.994
When exactly are we
doing the bombing?

17:48.028 --> 17:49.495
The attack will
happen tomorrow

17:49.529 --> 17:51.063
during afternoon
rush hour.

17:51.097 --> 17:53.030
And that's actually where
you come in, Peter.

17:53.065 --> 17:55.799
In order to get past the
checkpoint at the toll plaza,

17:55.833 --> 17:58.267
we will need an American
behind the wheel

17:58.301 --> 18:00.570
to arouse the least amount
of suspicion.

18:00.605 --> 18:01.971
Sorry, can you repeat all that?

18:02.005 --> 18:04.005
I just had an itch
right by my microphone.

18:04.039 --> 18:05.039
Microphone?!

18:06.108 --> 18:07.341
He's wearing a wire!

18:11.478 --> 18:13.212
Hey, Joe, can I ask
you a question?

18:13.247 --> 18:14.947
Can you fart?
Oh, of course I can.

18:14.982 --> 18:16.282
I've got a button
for it right here.

18:16.316 --> 18:17.816
(farting)

18:17.850 --> 18:18.850
Aw, cool!

18:18.885 --> 18:20.784
(Peter whimpering)

18:20.819 --> 18:22.719
Hold on. Oh, no!

18:22.753 --> 18:24.521
It sounds like they
found Peter's wire!

18:24.555 --> 18:26.221
Change of plans.

18:26.256 --> 18:28.590
The attack happens now.

18:36.330 --> 18:37.497
Now drive.

18:37.532 --> 18:39.365
Man, I never thought
it would end like this.

18:39.399 --> 18:41.066
Why, what did
you imagine?

18:41.101 --> 18:43.935
Basically the same thing,
only Nathan Lane.

18:43.969 --> 18:46.905
♪ Now, drive!

18:59.481 --> 19:00.948
Okay, you're
good to go.

19:05.286 --> 19:06.852
Pull over up here.

19:09.222 --> 19:11.489
Please, Mahmoud,
don't do this.

19:11.523 --> 19:12.557
It is too late.

19:12.591 --> 19:13.790
The job must be done.

19:13.824 --> 19:15.593
Look, I know you're mad
at our government,

19:15.627 --> 19:18.361
but you gotta realize,
that's only part of America.

19:18.396 --> 19:19.762
We're the land of the free

19:19.796 --> 19:21.964
and the home of the sunburnt,
freckled fat guy.

19:21.998 --> 19:24.265
A place where Jenny McCarthy
has a role

19:24.300 --> 19:26.266
in the debate over
childhood vaccinations.

19:26.301 --> 19:28.634
A country where you can walk
into any IHOP

19:28.669 --> 19:30.069
and see black women fighting.

19:30.103 --> 19:32.238
And where Ubu is considered
a good dog

19:32.272 --> 19:33.472
even though he never sat.

19:33.507 --> 19:35.473
We're the proud nation
where someone can

19:35.508 --> 19:37.509
shoot up their entire workplace
with a thing,

19:37.543 --> 19:40.344
and then the next day nobody
talks about banning that thing.

19:40.378 --> 19:42.545
It's the land that
lets people on Twitter

19:42.580 --> 19:44.646
spell the word "their"
any way they want.

19:44.681 --> 19:46.316
And where, if you think
you can dance,

19:46.350 --> 19:49.117
that assertion will be
challenged and evaluated.

19:49.152 --> 19:50.218
For we...

19:50.253 --> 19:51.886
are America.

19:51.920 --> 19:53.287
You will not convince me.

19:53.322 --> 19:55.722
America must pay for its sins!

19:59.259 --> 20:00.725
Hold it right there!

20:03.062 --> 20:05.096
Mahmoud, you're under arrest.

20:05.130 --> 20:07.531
Look, Joe,
I drove a van.

20:13.903 --> 20:16.538
Oh, Peter,
I'm so glad you're okay.

20:16.572 --> 20:18.239
Oh, me too, Lois.

20:18.274 --> 20:19.773
That was some
pretty rough stuff.

20:19.808 --> 20:22.809
You... you didn't
cry, did you?

20:22.843 --> 20:25.077
Well, I mean, I went
through an awful lot.

20:25.111 --> 20:27.546
Peter, if you cried,
we are done.

20:27.580 --> 20:29.080
Great job, Peter.

20:29.114 --> 20:31.414
Thanks to you, 30 terrorists are
behind bars,

20:31.449 --> 20:33.084
and every middle-class Arab
in this town

20:33.118 --> 20:35.051
is now under suspicion.

20:35.086 --> 20:36.052
So what
happens next,

20:36.087 --> 20:37.208
do those guys
all get trials?

20:37.221 --> 20:39.455
Well, you know...
(mumbling)

20:39.489 --> 20:42.790
(sighs) It's a long... it's the
process, and... whatever.

20:42.825 --> 20:44.057
Well, what do
you guys say

20:44.092 --> 20:45.726
we all go celebrate
at the Clam?

20:45.760 --> 20:46.892
That's a great idea.

20:46.927 --> 20:48.829
Yeah, I think we could
all use a drink.

20:48.863 --> 20:50.363
Tell you what,
let me call Horace

20:50.397 --> 20:52.598
and tell him to
get our table ready.

20:54.600 --> 20:56.567
Peter, did you just...
Let's go, let's go, let's go...

20:56.568 --> 21:57.568
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru